So the mechanic explained some of the things that you do when you get a tune-up.

45
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:39,040
So for example, he said that they change the motor oil.

46
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:43,780
Okay, so like it sounds, motor oil is oil for your motor.

47
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:44,520
That's right.

48
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:52,400
And there are other kinds of oil as well and oil is oftentimes put into the car and then sometimes it falls out.

49
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,680
And so what's that thing that catches the oil when it comes down?

50
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:57,520
It's called an oil pan.

51
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,920
So yes, as you said, there are different types of oils.

52
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:02,780
Cooking oil is obviously for cooking, for eating.

53
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,840
But motor oil is not for eating, it's for your motor.

54
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,120
But we also have to change the oil filter.

55
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:13,280
Now this is an important part that often gets mentioned at tune-ups.

56
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:13,440
That's right.

57
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,920
So the word filter here, you have the verb to filter.

58
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,580
In this case, we also have a noun, it's called a filter.

59
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:33,140
So what this device does, it collects maybe dirt or rocks and dust or anything that you don't want to be in your engine and specifically maybe if the oil is a little bit dirty.

60
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:40,260
Right, so an oil filter makes sure that the oil in your motor is not going to harm your motor.

61
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:44,760
And we also have a couple of interesting things like the fuel filter.

62
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:47,140
Now how is this different from the oil filter?

63
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,080
It's pretty much the same thing.

64
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:55,500
The only difference is that this filter specifically cleans the gasoline in your car.

65
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:56,900
Okay, similar object.

66
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,380
After that, we have something very different.

67
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,460
These are spark plugs.

68
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:01,600
That's right.

69
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:05,840
These are small little devices that, as the name says, create a spark.

70
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,380
This is how your engine goes.

71
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,540
This is how your car moves.

72
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,060
You have a spark and then everything starts running.

73
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,800
Spark plugs are actually quite important, right?

74
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:14,400
That's right.

75
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:21,320
So a spark is a very quick flash of light that comes out.

76
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:21,460
That's right.

77
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:22,460
It's not a long light.

78
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,320
It's just a spark.

79
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:30,720
So maybe when I strike a match or I use a lighter, there's a spark and that's what starts the fire.

80
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,000
That's right.

81
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,020
That's exactly right.

82
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,680
So a spark plug.

83
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:40,160
And now we also check the oil levels of our car and that's a very important thing as well.

84
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,080
Yeah, that's right.

85
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:53,040
So the oil level is something that you test with a long stick and you put it into the engine, the oil container, and make sure that there is enough oil because if there's not enough oil, you can have very serious car trouble.

86
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:53,840
That's right.

87
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:58,680
